# Feature Layout

## Purpose

Keep every feature module self-contained and predictable so navigation and reviews are fast.

## When Applied

Editing anything under `lib/features/**`.

## Requirements

New work lives under `lib/features/<feature>/`:

```
features/<name>/
  data/
    models/          # *_model.dart
    datasources/     # *_remote_ds.dart
    repositories/    # *_repository.dart (auth: *_repo.dart)
  domain/            # optional — required for auth-style contracts
  presentation/
    bloc/            # or cubit files
    pages/
    widgets/
```

- Extend an existing feature before creating a new top-level one.
- Cross-feature shared code goes in `lib/core/`, not another feature.
- Gold standard: `lib/features/auth` (full data/domain/presentation split).

## Examples

- New booking widget → `lib/features/booking/presentation/widgets/`.

## Anti-patterns

- Placing remote calls, models, or pages outside their layer folder.
- Reaching into another feature's `data/` directly instead of via `lib/core/`.

## Common Mistakes

- Adding a new feature folder for what is really a variant of `booking`/`sessions`.
- Growing `lib/view/` legacy screens instead of `lib/features/`.
